---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import "../styles/service.css";

const SITE = "https://www.tmdesignengineering.com";
const url = `${SITE}/for-founders`;
const jsonld = [
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "WebPage",
    "@id": `${url}#page`,
    url,
    name: "For Founders, a design engineer to build your product",
    isPartOf: { "@id": `${SITE}/#website` },
    about: { "@id": `${SITE}/#business` },
    description:
      "A design engineer for first-time founders: turn your idea into a real, manufacturable product with a steady process and honest guidance.",
  },
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
    itemListElement: [
      { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: `${SITE}/` },
      { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "For Founders", item: url },
    ],
  },
];
---
<Base
  title="For Founders, Turn Your Idea Into a Real Product | Thomas McKee"
  description="A design engineer for first-time founders. Turn your idea into a working, manufacturable product with a steady process, honest guidance and plain-English engineering. Start from £650."
  type="website"
  jsonld={jsonld}>
<main>
  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="svc-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow">For founders &amp; entrepreneurs</span>
      <h1>Turn your idea into <em>something real</em></h1>
      <p class="lede">Turning a product idea into a real, manufactured product is a long and complex journey with many unknowns. Working with me takes much of that risk and those unknowns out of the process. As someone who has done the whole product development journey multiple times, I take your idea and apply the same development structure, working with you to handle the technical side of launching a product. A steady process with professional guidance throughout.</p>
      <div class="svc-hero-cta">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/#contact">Book a free intro call <span class="arw">→</span></a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/services/feasibility-study">Start from £650</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PAIN -->
  <section class="band alt">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="sec-idx">If this sounds like you</span>
      <h2 class="sec-title">What are you stuck on?</h2>
      <div class="pain">
        <div class="q"><span class="mk">?</span><p>"I have an idea, but no idea what it will cost or how long it will take."</p></div>
        <div class="q"><span class="mk">?</span><p>"I'm not an engineer. Will I actually understand what's going on and why?"</p></div>
        <div class="q"><span class="mk">?</span><p>"How do I know if this is even possible before I spend real money?"</p></div>
      </div>
      <p class="sec-intro">All three are the right questions, and all three are answerable early, so that you know exactly what you're starting. The whole way I work is built around removing that uncertainty early on and cheaply, so that you don't invest time, effort and money into something that doesn't work.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- HOW I HELP -->
  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="sec-idx">Where to start</span>
      <h2 class="sec-title">Services for early stages</h2>
      <p class="sec-intro">Most founders begin with one of these two. A study to find out if the idea holds up, or, once it does, a prototype development service that turns it into a working MVP.</p>
      <div class="aud-grid">
        <a class="aud" href="/services/feasibility-study">
          <div class="aud-top"><h3>Feasibility Study</h3><span class="aud-price">from £650</span></div>
          <p>Technical validation is as important as commercial validation: know if it can be built, and the costs involved, before real investment.</p>
          <span class="aud-go">Feasibility Study <span class="arw">→</span></span>
        </a>
        <a class="aud" href="/services/concept-mvp-development">
          <div class="aud-top"><h3>Concept &amp; MVP Development</h3><span class="aud-tag">Founder favourite</span></div>
          <p>Turn the idea into an evaluated, buildable concept and a working MVP you can put in front of users, test, and raise investment on.</p>
          <span class="aud-go">Concept &amp; MVP <span class="arw">→</span></span>
        </a>
      </div>
      <p class="sec-intro" style="margin-top:22px">When you want it taken the whole way, I offer <a href="/services/product-development" style="color:var(--ember)">full Product Development</a>. It means one engineer owns the path from idea to a product that's ready to manufacture, in scoped phases, so we can go through the product development process steadily and smoothly.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- WHY ME -->
  <section class="band alt">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="sec-idx">Why founders work with me</span>
      <h2 class="sec-title">My way of working is built for someone developing their first product</h2>
      <div class="deliv">
        <div class="di"><div class="dn">01</div><h3>Plain-English engineering</h3><p>The decisions and the trade-offs explained clearly, without gatekeeping the technical side. You always understand where your product stands and why.</p></div>
        <div class="di"><div class="dn">02</div><h3>Structure &amp; rhythm</h3><p>A steady, proven process that walks you through an industry-standard development journey, keeping momentum with a clear plan and preventing costly mistakes.</p></div>
        <div class="di"><div class="dn">03</div><h3>A passion for making meaningful products</h3><p>Designing new products and putting new ideas out into the world is really exciting to me. If we work together, you can guarantee I'll be committed to getting something made. If I don't think the project will work, I'll be honest about that, and about the different options that might.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="svc-cred">
        <span class="ci">Behind <b>award-winning</b> consumer products, including the Red Dot Ooni Volt 2</span>
        <span class="ci"><b>Concept to volume manufacture</b>, held end to end</span>
        <span class="ci">Start from a <b>£50 Power Hour</b> or a <b>£650 study</b></span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="band" id="start">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="cta">
        <div class="inner">
          <span class="eyebrow">Let's talk</span>
          <h2 style="margin-top:14px">Have an idea you want to make real?</h2>
          <p>Book a free intro call and tell me about it. I'll be honest about whether I can help and what a sensible, low-risk first step looks like for you.</p>
          <div class="row">
            <a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" href="/#contact">Book a free intro call <span class="arw">→</span></a>
            <span class="price-tag">Or start with a <b>£50 Power Hour</b></span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
<style>
  .aud-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:16px;margin-top:26px}
  @media(max-width:760px){.aud-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
  .aud{display:flex;flex-direction:column;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:14px;background:var(--surface);padding:24px 26px;text-decoration:none;transition:.15s}
  .aud:hover{border-color:var(--ink-3);transform:translateY(-2px)}
  .aud-top{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:baseline;gap:12px}
  .aud h3{font-size:1.18rem;letter-spacing:-0.015em;color:var(--ink)}
  .aud p{color:var(--ink-2);font-size:0.98rem;margin-top:10px;line-height:1.5;flex:1}
  .aud-price{font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:12px;color:var(--ember);flex:none}
  .aud-tag{font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:0.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ember);border:1px solid var(--ember);border-radius:20px;padding:2px 9px;flex:none}
  .aud-go{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;margin-top:18px;font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:12.5px;color:var(--ember)}
</style>
</Base>
